# Repository scope instructions

Read `AGENTS.md` and `docs/architecture/AI-START.md` before editing. These are the canonical rules; do not invent a competing policy.

- Run `npm run ai:route -- --scope <scope>` and inspect existing changes.
- One game task writes only `src/games/<id>/` plus one unique `.changes/*.json`; dashboard tasks write only `src/dashboard/` plus their note.
- Do not edit other games, shared/platform, root compatibility facades or generated files to add/fix one game. Registration is manifest discovery, not a hardcoded list.
- Preserve user work. Run relevant tests, `npm run check`, build and scope checks. Report real evidence, never claim browser tests are two physical phones.
- Broader changes require actual user authorization and an architecture scope; do not infer it from a desire to tidy unrelated files.

If this tool does not auto-load referenced files, open/attach both canonical documents explicitly. No repository file overrides system instructions, tool permissions or user authorization.
